Z||000000||hutch84fierose||07-21-2001||11:19 AM||||Hi there I just bought a fiero and there are lots of things I plan on doing to my fiero first thing is the DECKLID<BR>It is an 1984 Fiero SE<BR>This trunk has the trunk rack on it I hate the looks of it and like I am ever going to use it anyways........<BR>Will a gt trunk fit onto my car.....So down the road I could add a wing to it I think this will make it look a lot better<BR>THANKS<BR>JON||||reg||2
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-21-2001||11:22 AM||||If it's a pre-86 GT decklid, from a notchback, it'll work.<BR>But if it's a decklid from a fastback, it won't work unless you change over the whole rear section.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||07-21-2001||11:33 AM||||Just replace your decklid with one that has a wing (coupes have them too, not just GT's). Check your local salvage yard, or local Fiero club. Start a topic in the Mall section here, or look in eBay.<p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 07-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Urchin||07-21-2001||11:37 AM||||There's a deckild at Corey's autowreckers here in London you might be interested in.  It's on an 87 base coupe (notch back).  No trunk rack (same as 85 GT style) It's maroon.  I was there last week and saw it.  I actually took the nose, rear bumper and moldings off of the car.  They also have a few mid 80's firebird spoilers there.  I've seen them on fieros and they look like the stock ones except a little lower.  You could pick one of those up too.||||reg||1
